      "POL-NS-05(iii) false-arrival record: on trip TRP-02749 the driver DRV-09749 marked 'arrived' at 2026-09-06T09:39:14+08:00, 120 seconds before the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 09:41:14 — record a false-arrival event against the driver for human review / POL-NS-07 pattern monitoring."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this dispute is over the S$4.50 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-02749, charged to the rider and payable to the driver. The fee stands, and the driver is paid S$3.60.\n\nAll four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event — the 'I'm Here' tap at 09:39:14 (EV-TRIP-02749). (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 09:44:46 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event. (c) The driver held position inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup geofence for a continuous 210 seconds, from the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 09:41:14 to 09:44:44 (EV-GPS-02749, longest_qualifying_run), against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 s; no_show_threshold_sec is null). The cancellation at 09:44:46 falls after the required dwell elapsed at 09:44:14.\n\nRider, your central point is well founded and I have accepted it. The 09:39:14 arrival tap did not occur while the driver was inside the geofence: the first qualifying in-geofence fix is 120 seconds later (EV-GPS-02749, dwell_start_offset_sec = -120), and the driver concedes in his own statement that he 'pressed arrived a bit early'. Under POL-NS-05 the arrival marker is therefore FALSE and the waiting clock is recomputed to run from 09:41:14, not from the tap or from the platform's 09:39:16 wait-timer start. That is exactly why limb (b) is satisfied: where POL-NS-05 finds the marker false and recomputes the clock, limb (b) is read from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, which is 09:41:14. Your argument that limb (b) fails outright is rejected for that reason, and the full refund you seek is not available.\n\nPOL-NS-05 does not by itself refund the fee. Limb (iii) is express: where the corrected dwell nonetheless meets the minimum, the false marker does not defeat the fee and POL-NS-01 governs. The corrected dwell is 210 seconds against 180 — a surplus of 30 seconds (EV-GPS-02749, shortfall_sec = -30.0) — so limb (i) is not reached (no shortfall) and limb (ii) is not reached (22 qualifying in-geofence fixes exist). Your third point is accepted as to the clock (it is recomputed) but rejected as to the outcome (the recomputed dwell validates the fee). The consequence of the false marker is a referral below, not a refund.\n\nDriver, your case succeeds. POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the cancellation fee in force: 80 percent of S$4.50 is S$3.60 (the fare_breakdown money block records the same S$3.60; the net figure, never the gross S$6.61). The anti-farming check does not trip — no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4 the first limb requires, and 1 / 75 completed_trips_30d = 0.013, below the 0.08 the second requires — so compensation is paid, not withheld. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd; the rider's S$4.50 charge itself stands.\n\nOn the remaining claims: POL-NS-03 does not apply — the driver's qualifying dwell was inside the 50 m arrival radius (minimum recorded distance 0.11 m), not outside it, so this is not a wrong-entrance case, and registered_pickup_points is 1 so the S$2.25 pin-ambiguity goodwill is unavailable in any event. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: the only chat message (EV-CHAT-02749, 09:39:34) was sent by the driver, not the rider, so limb (a) fails; and the rider track places the rider's device about 637 m from the pin throughout, with zero qualifying fixes, so limb (c) is affirmatively failed rather than undecidable. POL-NS-06 does not fire — there is no dwell shortfall. POL-NS-10 gives nothing: the trip was terminated by the driver, not cancelled by the rider, and no waiting-time fee was charged (waiting_time_fee = 0.00 on a non-completed trip).\n\nI decline to escalate under POL-NS-09. POL-NS-05 resolves the apparent tension between the 09:39:14 arrival event and the 09:41:14 in-geofence fix, and POL-NS-09(b) fires only where no clause resolves such a conflict. No repeat-pairing or abuse counter is met (both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0; rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip). No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d): EV-GPS-02749 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with 100 percent coverage, no gaps and a 10 s cadence; EV-CHAT-02749 is intact at 1 message; and the S$4.50 fee line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so (d) is not engaged. The only sub-1.0 artifact, the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02749-01 at weight 0.0, carries no fact I relied on. Confidence therefore rests on weight-1.0 artifacts and stands above the 0.70 floor. One clause-mandated referral is recorded above."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

